  "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{11\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{24}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(12n+25)\\pi }{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\u2026,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-2$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=\\frac{13\\pi }{24}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24},\\frac{13\\pi }{24}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\cdot \\frac{13\\pi }{24}=\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}.\n$$",
